- For all `i` in `[0, index)`, `this.get(i)` after the call equals `\old(this.get(i))`.

Using the rules:
- Use `\old(...)` to refer to values before the method call.
- Use `\forall` for universal quantification.
- Use `=>` for implication.

Final assert statement:

<code>assert 0 <= index && index < \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>
